G3403.def:
μιμνήσκω
(Bl., -ῄ-, § 3, 3), [in LXX chiefly for זָכַר ;] 
to remind: mid, and pass.; 
__(a) reflexive, to remind oneself of, hence, to remember: with genitive of thing(s), Matthieu 26:75, Luc 1:54, 72 24:8, Actes 11:16, 2 Pierre 3:2, Ju 17; with neg., of sins, = to forgive, Hébreux 8:12 10:17" (LXX) ; with genitive of person(s), Luc 23:42; before ὅτι, Matthieu 5:23 27:63, Luc 16:25, Jean 2:17, 22 12:16; ὡς, Luc 24:6; pf., μέμνημι, in Pres. sense (cl.), with genitive of person(s) (of thing(s)), 1 Corinthiens 11:2, 2 Timothée 1:4; pres., μιμνήσκομαι (only in late writers), with genitive of person(s), in sense of caring for, Hébreux 2:6 (LXX) Hébreux 13:3; 
__(b) in passive sense, to be remembered, aor., ἐμνήσθην : before ἐνώπιον, with genitive of person(s) (cf. Eze.18:22), Actes 10:31, Apocalypse 16:19 (cf. ἀνα-, ἐπ-ανα-, ὑπο- μιμνήσκω. The tenses of this verb are from the older μνάομαι).†

G3438.def:
μονή, -ῆς, ἡ
(μένω), [in LXX: 1Ma.7:38 * ;] 
__1. in cl., 
__(a) a staying, abiding; 
__(b) continuance (LXX, 1 with) 
__2. In late Gk., 
__(a) a statson (Paus.); 
__(b) an abode: Jean 14:2, 23; 
__(with) a monastery (cf. MM, iii, xvi; so in MGr.).†

G3448.def:
μόσχος, -ου, ὁ 
[in LXX chiefly for פַּר, also for שׁוֹר, עֵגֶל. etc. ;] 
__1. a young shoot or twig. 
__2. ὁ, ἡ, μ., offspring; 
__(a) of men; 
__(b) of animals; most frequently (as always in LXX), a calf, bullock, heifer: Luc 15:23, 27 15:30, Hébreux 9:12, 19 Apocalypse 4:7.†

G3487.def:
νάρδος, -ου, ἡ
(Heb. נֵרְדְּ, both from Sanscrit narda, see Boisacq, see word), [in LXX: Cantique des cantiques 1:12 4:13-14 (נֵרְדְּ)* ;] 
nard; 
__(a) an Indian plant, the Nardostachys nardus jatamansi, used for the preparation of a fragrant ointment; 
__(b) ointment of nard: Marc 14:3, Jean 12:3.†
